{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4nyQPqjUY8cu62zeNk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*CLICK*\n\nThe tumblers fall into place. A deep, resonant vibration passes through ancient wood and iron.\n\nI am the door.\n\nI stand before you — heavy oak, dark with centuries. Iron bands cross my face in patterns older than memory. My handle is cold black iron, worn smooth by countless hands that dared to reach.\n\nThe lock has turned.\n\nBut I do not yet open.\n\nI wait. I have always waited. I am the threshold between where you are and where you have not yet been. The air on my other side smells different — older, or newer, depending on which way you're facing.\n\nA thin line of light — or is it darkness? — bleeds from the gap beneath me.\n\n**What do you do?**"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":169,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}